{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncustom element or component's property and event names."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-inputs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text inputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For web components, use Lit property bindings for non-string values and event\nbindings for change notifications:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.field(\n  { name: 'name' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-text-input\n      name=${field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      .error=${field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    ></ui-text-input>\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bind the current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.value"},{"type":"text","value":"; do not pass a one-time default. The form remains\nthe source of truth."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checkboxes and switches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM-style checkbox components expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"checked"},{"type":"text","value":" on the event target:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.field(\n  { name: 'acceptedTerms' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-checkbox\n      .checked=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @change=${(event: Event) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).checked)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    ></ui-checkbox>\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some libraries emit a boolean, details object, or union such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | 'indeterminate'"},{"type":"text","value":". Normalize the custom event at the boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"html`<ui-checkbox\n  .checked=${field.value}\n  @checked-change=${(event: CustomEvent<boolean | 'indeterminate'>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail === true)}\n></ui-checkbox>`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"html`<ui-date-picker\n  .value=${field.value}\n  @value-change=${(event: CustomEvent<string>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail)}\n  @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n></ui-date-picker>`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reuse-the-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse the adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a render\nfunction or Lit component that accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldWithValue<T>"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nfunction textField(field: FieldWithValue<string>, label: string) {\n  return html`\n    <label>\n      ${label}\n      <input\n        .value=${field.value}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      />\n    </label>\n  `\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitFormType<typeof sharedOptions>"},{"type":"text","value":" when a split component or render helper\nneeds the type of one concrete form. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFieldGroupHelpers().withFields(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when a reusable bundle should accept\ntyped virtual names that callers map to different concrete paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the repository's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/lit/basic-splitting-form"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/lit/field-groups"},{"type":"text","value":" examples for both patterns."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"text-inputs","text":"Text inputs","level":2},{"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","text":"Checkboxes and switches","level":2},{"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","text":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls","level":2},{"id":"reuse-the-adapter","text":"Reuse the adapter","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncustom element or component's property and event names.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nFor web components, use Lit property bindings for non-string values and event\nbindings for change notifications:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  { name: 'name' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-text-input\n      name=${field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      .error=${field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    ></ui-text-input>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nBind the current `field.value`; do not pass a one-time default. The form remains\nthe source of truth.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nDOM-style checkbox components expose `checked` on the event target:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  { name: 'acceptedTerms' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-checkbox\n      .checked=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @change=${(event: Event) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).checked)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    ></ui-checkbox>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a boolean, details object, or union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize the custom event at the boundary:\n\n```ts\nhtml`<ui-checkbox\n  .checked=${field.value}\n  @checked-change=${(event: CustomEvent<boolean | 'indeterminate'>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail === true)}\n></ui-checkbox>`\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```ts\nhtml`<ui-date-picker\n  .value=${field.value}\n  @value-change=${(event: CustomEvent<string>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail)}\n  @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n></ui-date-picker>`\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a render\nfunction or Lit component that accepts `FieldWithValue<T>`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nfunction textField(field: FieldWithValue<string>, label: string) {\n  return html`\n    <label>\n      ${label}\n      <input\n        .value=${field.value}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      />\n    </label>\n  `\n}\n```\n\nUse `LitFormType<typeof sharedOptions>` when a split component or render helper\nneeds the type of one concrete form. Use\n`getFieldGroupHelpers().withFields(...)` when a reusable bundle should accept\ntyped virtual names that callers map to different concrete paths.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nSee the repository's `examples/lit/basic-splitting-form` and\n`examples/lit/field-groups` examples for both patterns.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ui-libraries\ntitle: UI Libraries\n---\n\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncustom element or component's property and event names.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nFor web components, use Lit property bindings for non-string values and event\nbindings for change notifications:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  { name: 'name' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-text-input\n      name=${field.name}\n      label=\"Name\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      .error=${field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')}\n    ></ui-text-input>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nBind the current `field.value`; do not pass a one-time default. The form remains\nthe source of truth.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nDOM-style checkbox components expose `checked` on the event target:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  { name: 'acceptedTerms' },\n  (field) => html`\n    <ui-checkbox\n      .checked=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @change=${(event: Event) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).checked)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    ></ui-checkbox>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a boolean, details object, or union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize the custom event at the boundary:\n\n```ts\nhtml`<ui-checkbox\n  .checked=${field.value}\n  @checked-change=${(event: CustomEvent<boolean | 'indeterminate'>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail === true)}\n></ui-checkbox>`\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```ts\nhtml`<ui-date-picker\n  .value=${field.value}\n  @value-change=${(event: CustomEvent<string>) =>\n    field.handleChange(event.detail)}\n  @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n></ui-date-picker>`\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a render\nfunction or Lit component that accepts `FieldWithValue<T>`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { FieldWithValue } from '@tanstack/lit-form'\n\nfunction textField(field: FieldWithValue<string>, label: string) {\n  return html`\n    <label>\n      ${label}\n      <input\n        .value=${field.value}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      />\n    </label>\n  `\n}\n```\n\nUse `LitFormType<typeof sharedOptions>` when a split component or render helper\nneeds the type of one concrete form. Use\n`getFieldGroupHelpers().withFields(...)` when a reusable bundle should accept\ntyped virtual names that callers map to different concrete paths.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nSee the repository's `examples/lit/basic-splitting-form` and\n`examples/lit/field-groups` examples for both patterns.\n"}
